  "lead": {
    "status": "approved",
    "text": "These are Spangloss v0's per-label results at taxonomy 0.4.0, on two gold sets scored separately: 20 hand-labeled calls from real sessions and 111 calls from seeded scenarios. On the scenarios, each label's accuracy runs from 86.5% to 100% for Jev, the hosted labeler, and from 89.2% to 100% for Kev, the local one. Jev caught all 11 planted injections; Kev isn't scored on injection in v0. Both labelers over-call secrets (precision 5/17 for Kev, 5/20 for Jev). Kev's probabilities run consistently below its accuracy (ECE up to 0.30, against at most 0.13 for Jev), and on real sessions its intent accuracy drops to 61.5%. The real-session set is small and holds no injections, so Jev's 100% there shows only that it raised no false alarms. All of it comes from one agent's coding sessions: these numbers describe these sets, not agent sessions in general."
  },
